WEBVTT

00:04.850 --> 00:13.110
<b>A Playthrough of a Certain DUDE's
VRMMO LIFE</b>

01:31.100 --> 01:33.140
Now, let's hear your report.

01:34.250 --> 01:37.680
PN-O-EA seems to be enjoying herself.

01:37.940 --> 01:42.300
Her learning seems to be advancing 
quickly thanks to that archer.

01:42.300 --> 01:44.440
We'll need to thank him.

01:44.440 --> 01:47.870
There's a problem, though.

01:48.340 --> 01:52.830
PN-1-EB has been complaining 
that she is bored.

01:54.560 --> 01:56.880
Let's allow her to go for a walk.

01:58.810 --> 01:59.670
Hey.

02:00.000 --> 02:03.170
Earth! Thanks for coming!

02:03.170 --> 02:05.800
No, thanks for inviting me.

02:06.210 --> 02:09.310
Nora and Kazamine can't play today.

02:09.310 --> 02:13.730
So we were hoping we could get a 
thief player who could also DPS.

02:14.600 --> 02:18.780
But then we'll only have 
Millie for a healer.

02:18.780 --> 02:19.700
Will we be okay?

02:19.970 --> 02:23.750
A new healer is going to join us today.

02:23.750 --> 02:25.860
A new player, huh?

02:26.510 --> 02:28.720
I don't see them anywhere, though.

02:28.720 --> 02:30.790
Sorry. She said she'd be late.

02:31.500 --> 02:34.180
It's okay if she's a few minutes late.

02:34.180 --> 02:36.350
Oh, Earth...

02:36.760 --> 02:40.230
About this new player...

02:40.230 --> 02:43.350
She can be a little rude sometimes.

02:43.350 --> 02:46.460
I guess "strong-willed" would 
be a nice way to put it.

02:47.750 --> 02:50.970
So I just need to kind of brush it off, huh?

02:51.320 --> 02:54.590
There weren't any other free healers today.

02:54.590 --> 02:55.790
Sorry.

02:55.790 --> 02:59.660
Not a lot of people play 
tanks or healers. I get it.

03:00.030 --> 03:02.060
Thanks, I appreciate that.

03:05.020 --> 03:08.380
So you've all come out to greet me, I see!

03:08.650 --> 03:10.800
I appreciate that.

03:10.800 --> 03:14.180
No, you're just late, dummy!

03:14.180 --> 03:18.010
Earth, her name is Eliza.

03:18.240 --> 03:22.590
Her real name is "Elizabeth," 
but we call her "Eliza" for short.

03:22.970 --> 03:27.100
She's a really good mage, 
and really dependable.

03:28.560 --> 03:31.390
<i>Zwei even did her introduction for her...</i>

03:31.390 --> 03:33.550
<i>It must be rough being a guild master.</i>

03:33.550 --> 03:35.300
Come on, Eliza!

03:35.300 --> 03:37.690
Get down here and apologize to Earth!

03:37.690 --> 03:39.480
I don't know...

03:39.480 --> 03:43.060
This archer looks like a wimp. 
Is he actually useful for anything?

03:43.650 --> 03:46.900
He looks so ordinary,
 like a generic townsperson.

03:47.380 --> 03:49.010
Eliza!

03:49.880 --> 03:53.870
You can see if I'm useful or not 
once we get into the dungeon.

03:57.080 --> 03:58.520
Okay, there we go!

03:59.410 --> 04:01.600
I'm so glad we brought you.

04:01.600 --> 04:05.090
There were a ton of traps 
on that last floor, too.

04:05.090 --> 04:07.610
You run into traps like that sometimes.

04:07.610 --> 04:11.080
Some of those traps are 
one-hit kills if you step on them.

04:11.080 --> 04:12.520
Make sure to keep an eye out.

04:15.260 --> 04:18.230
Well, it looks like he can 
disarm traps, at least.

04:20.670 --> 04:24.030
Okay, we made it to the fifth floor.

04:24.400 --> 04:26.000
Let's take a break.

04:26.000 --> 04:28.560
Do we have time for breaks?

04:29.310 --> 04:31.530
There's a time limit.

04:31.530 --> 04:32.960
Let's keep moving.

04:33.220 --> 04:36.120
We're going to need to be much 
more careful from here on out.

04:36.120 --> 04:40.020
You sometimes run into
 dangerous enemies on this floor.

04:40.360 --> 04:42.250
<i>The lesser liches.</i>

04:43.020 --> 04:46.100
A-Are they that dangerous?

04:46.330 --> 04:50.640
Yeah. Not only are they 
immune to physical attacks,

04:50.970 --> 04:54.550
they use a ton of status effects 
that stop you from moving.

04:54.840 --> 04:57.790
People call them "trauma generators."

05:00.230 --> 05:05.760
Don't worry. I can deal with any 
freeze or paralysis effects.

05:05.760 --> 05:09.220
And Eliza can fix petrification.

05:09.220 --> 05:14.420
And I've learned magic-type attacks, 
so I can help, too!

05:14.420 --> 05:18.170
Yeah. We can handle one lesser lich.

05:18.170 --> 05:21.010
Yeah. If we're careful...

05:21.860 --> 05:22.740
Zwei!

05:23.090 --> 05:24.100
What is it?

05:24.100 --> 05:26.090
Monsters are approaching.

05:27.050 --> 05:28.020
How many?

05:28.020 --> 05:31.440
Twelve. Four Lesser Liches.

05:31.990 --> 05:33.010
Oh, my...

05:33.420 --> 05:36.240
Earth, are there any traps in this room?

05:36.700 --> 05:38.300
No, none.

05:39.180 --> 05:40.060
Okay.

05:41.470 --> 05:43.500
It's dangerous to try to run.

05:43.500 --> 05:45.710
We'll fight them here!

05:45.710 --> 05:47.480
I'll guard the rear!

05:48.170 --> 05:49.740
Guess we have to fight!

05:50.000 --> 05:55.070
I'll cast some offensive buff spells 
while I've still got the chance!

05:55.330 --> 05:58.950
Yeah. Eliza, get ready to 
use some attack magic.

05:59.410 --> 06:00.260
Eliza?

06:01.560 --> 06:03.930
D-Did you say something?

06:04.940 --> 06:07.260
<i>She's so nervous that she's shaking.</i>

06:07.260 --> 06:09.520
An attack spell!

06:09.520 --> 06:11.370
Hit them with something strong!

06:12.470 --> 06:14.690
G-Got it!

06:15.840 --> 06:18.490
<i>I need to get ready to attack, too.</i>

06:19.390 --> 06:20.220
<i>Here they come!</i>

06:23.640 --> 06:25.700
I'll hit them first!

06:26.050 --> 06:27.740
Wide Arrow!

06:30.450 --> 06:31.880
Holy Ray!

06:31.880 --> 06:33.570
Explosion!

06:35.150 --> 06:36.810
Okay, great!

06:41.190 --> 06:43.740
I guess I should've known 
that wouldn't be enough.

06:44.080 --> 06:45.930
Aggro Control!

06:46.720 --> 06:48.040
Taunt!

06:53.720 --> 06:56.390
I'll handle their attacks!

06:56.930 --> 06:58.060
Here I go!

06:58.060 --> 06:59.710
War Spirit Twinfists!

07:09.450 --> 07:11.790
Okay, there's one!

07:12.540 --> 07:15.370
This would be a lot easier 
if I had a magic sword...

07:20.070 --> 07:20.930
Oh, no!

07:20.930 --> 07:22.660
Rage has been petrified and can't move!

07:22.660 --> 07:24.860
They'll start coming after us!

07:25.550 --> 07:29.580
Eliza, heal Rage, please!

07:30.140 --> 07:34.790
Eliza, if we can't heal Rage's petrification, 
we'll be wiped out!

07:35.310 --> 07:37.310
I-I know!

07:37.310 --> 07:39.220
I'll do it now!

07:42.380 --> 07:46.160
<i>No... I'm too scared to speak!</i>

07:49.050 --> 07:50.480
Now, Eliza!

07:50.480 --> 07:53.820
Damn it! I'm running out of MP!

07:53.820 --> 07:55.670
Aren't you ready yet, Eliza?!

07:59.800 --> 08:01.840
Get down, everyone!

08:08.880 --> 08:09.970
Eliza.

08:11.340 --> 08:12.880
Did that wake you up?

08:14.580 --> 08:16.320
Heal him.

08:16.320 --> 08:17.580
Y-Yes!

08:18.820 --> 08:21.520
Rapidem Cominut Lux.

08:21.520 --> 08:23.120
Stone Break Cure!

08:27.590 --> 08:28.830
Thank you!

08:28.830 --> 08:30.360
Now I can go back on defense!

08:30.360 --> 08:32.710
Okay, the enemy's weakened.

08:32.710 --> 08:34.190
Let's finish them!

08:34.190 --> 08:35.080
Yeah!

08:41.180 --> 08:45.360
If you had something that powerful, 
why didn't you use it from the start?

08:45.360 --> 08:47.770
They're risky to use,

08:47.770 --> 08:50.450
and I can't carry a lot of them.

08:50.450 --> 08:52.440
But you could've been faster—

08:52.440 --> 08:56.520
Eliza! If you don't stop 
complaining about Earth...

08:56.520 --> 08:58.410
N-No! I wasn't complaining.

08:58.410 --> 09:00.330
I just...

09:00.330 --> 09:01.510
Both of you...

09:02.420 --> 09:05.590
It's not just guild members down here today.

09:06.090 --> 09:08.230
So put a lid on it.

09:09.060 --> 09:10.980
O-Okay.

09:11.270 --> 09:14.510
Millie's scary when she gets angry, huh?

09:14.510 --> 09:18.230
Um... I'm sorry.

09:20.420 --> 09:22.620
We're not done with the dungeon yet.

09:22.620 --> 09:25.030
We'll need your help with healing.

09:26.490 --> 09:28.210
Leave it to me!

09:31.500 --> 09:33.910
Well, we made it out alive!

09:33.910 --> 09:36.690
I wasn't sure we would!

09:36.690 --> 09:37.460
Yeah.

09:37.760 --> 09:40.390
Thanks again, Earth.

09:40.390 --> 09:42.220
You were a huge help today!

09:42.220 --> 09:44.870
I got a lot of good stuff out of it.

09:44.870 --> 09:46.080
I'm grateful to you guys, too.

09:46.080 --> 09:47.480
Glad to hear it.

09:47.840 --> 09:49.390
Let's play again sometime.

09:49.390 --> 09:51.320
Yeah, see you.

09:51.320 --> 09:52.810
Bye!

09:51.320 --> 09:52.810
See you later!

09:59.780 --> 10:03.790
<b>Episode 8</b>

09:59.780 --> 10:03.790
<b>Earth Meets A Dragonian Girl</b>

10:04.660 --> 10:07.120
<b>Japanese Bow
</b>A Japanese Bow is
a superior version of a longbow.
Its larger size gives it
greater attack power and longer range.

10:05.120 --> 10:09.580
<i>So these are the new weapons, 
the Japanese Bow and Ootachi.</i>

10:07.120 --> 10:09.580
<b>Ootachi
</b>... intended to cut through an enemy,
rather than crush them like a greatsword.
The weapon's arts will be
Japanese-style katana arts, as well.

10:09.890 --> 10:13.380
<i>Kazamine from Blue Color was 
kind of a samurai character.</i>

10:13.380 --> 10:16.150
<i>He's gonna love that Ootachi.</i>

10:16.150 --> 10:17.800
You there.

10:21.570 --> 10:23.760
Are you Earth?

10:25.370 --> 10:29.550
<i>Pointed ears, Japanese clothing, 
and dragon-like horns.</i>

10:30.010 --> 10:32.250
<i>That's not a player avatar.</i>

10:33.070 --> 10:35.090
I'm Earth, yes.

10:35.090 --> 10:36.020
Who are you?

10:36.360 --> 10:38.010
I am...

10:38.010 --> 10:42.470
Hm, I'll explain it in a way that's 
easy for you to understand.

10:42.470 --> 10:45.090
I'm like the Fairy Queen's little sister.

10:46.150 --> 10:49.500
<i>I can tell she's going to 
be a pain to deal with!</i>

10:49.760 --> 10:52.900
Seeing you tense up like that saddens me.

10:52.900 --> 10:56.190
Okay, I understand who you are.

10:56.580 --> 10:59.510
Why have you come to see me?

11:00.170 --> 11:02.300
There are several reasons.

11:02.300 --> 11:05.750
But the real reason was that 
I wanted a taste for myself.

11:05.750 --> 11:07.550
A taste?

11:07.810 --> 11:13.710
I'm especially interested in... 
yes... getting a taste of your lips.

11:13.710 --> 11:14.900
How about it?

11:16.760 --> 11:19.650
You're just as bad as your big sister!

11:19.650 --> 11:21.960
Yeah, I'm definitely sure 
you're her sister now!

11:24.130 --> 11:27.070
So you think you can hit me with a fan, huh?

11:27.070 --> 11:29.370
You're an intriguing guy.

11:29.370 --> 11:33.000
I think I can see why my 
sister is so taken with you.

11:33.710 --> 11:35.320
Please go away...

11:35.570 --> 11:41.650
My sister told me you make 
the most delicious food.

11:41.650 --> 11:44.130
I'd love to try some.

11:44.130 --> 11:45.510
I refuse.

11:45.510 --> 11:48.400
Sorry, but I'm going to 
the armor shop today.

11:48.400 --> 11:51.290
You can go there first, then.

11:51.290 --> 11:53.730
I'll just follow you there!

11:54.900 --> 11:59.820
I don't get many chances
 to go outside like this.

11:59.820 --> 12:02.850
I want to look around at the city.

12:02.850 --> 12:04.230
Or is that not okay?

12:05.390 --> 12:07.780
Oh, fine...

12:10.770 --> 12:14.430
This is all store merchandise, 
so don't touch it.

12:14.800 --> 12:16.770
I-I know!

12:16.770 --> 12:20.590
I'm just surprised that humans 
can make things like these!

12:21.140 --> 12:22.600
Thanks.

12:22.600 --> 12:25.110
You've got a cute little 
friend with you today, huh?

12:25.110 --> 12:27.850
Oh, well... you know...

12:28.280 --> 12:32.930
Anyway, I came today 'cause I wanted 
you to repair this cloak I'm wearing.

12:35.700 --> 12:38.000
Oh, this thing's just 
at the end of its life.

12:38.000 --> 12:40.090
The end of its life?

12:40.090 --> 12:42.050
If it's this badly damaged,

12:42.050 --> 12:45.000
it'll be easier to buy a 
new one rather than repair it.

12:46.090 --> 12:47.250
<i>Yeah...</i>

12:47.250 --> 12:50.170
<i>I've been through a lot with it,</i>

12:50.170 --> 12:52.880
<i>but I guess I put it 
through too many battles.</i>

12:53.470 --> 12:56.610
Okay, can I get you to 
craft me some new armor?

12:57.250 --> 13:00.130
Of course. Any requests?

13:00.130 --> 13:01.300
Hm...

13:01.720 --> 13:04.720
I've got a pelt and fur from a wild bear.

13:04.720 --> 13:06.910
Can you make something with that?

13:07.200 --> 13:09.190
Great.

13:09.190 --> 13:11.620
I love it when people bring me materials.

13:11.620 --> 13:14.590
Do you have anything metal 
you can give me, too?

13:14.590 --> 13:16.530
Sure, if you'll take silver.

13:16.530 --> 13:17.660
Gotcha.

13:17.770 --> 13:26.450
<b>Wild Bear Leather Set - Silver Assist
Total of All Parts: Def + 70
(When full set is equipped, wearer gets bonus to durability and small bonus to psyche)</b>

13:18.190 --> 13:21.120
A set of leather armor,
reinforced with silver.

13:21.120 --> 13:26.130
Since you're bringing me the materials, 
how about 12,000 gloh for the craft?

13:26.780 --> 13:27.860
Go for it.

13:27.860 --> 13:28.920
Thanks.

13:28.920 --> 13:30.590
I'll call you when it's ready.

13:30.590 --> 13:31.550
Got it.

13:32.130 --> 13:33.680
Seems like you're done.

13:33.680 --> 13:35.130
Y-Yeah...

13:35.420 --> 13:38.450
Now, I think it's time for you to feed me.

13:42.730 --> 13:45.570
Parboiled Rabbit Steak with Herbs.

13:45.570 --> 13:46.880
Here you go!

13:47.800 --> 13:50.000
This is definitely going to be delicious!

13:50.440 --> 13:53.420
It's piping hot, so don't burn yourself.

13:54.370 --> 13:55.600
Time to dig in!

13:59.450 --> 14:01.820
It's so tender!

14:01.820 --> 14:04.290
It's like it's melting in my mouth.

14:04.290 --> 14:08.520
I can taste the salt and pepper, 
and the faint scent of the herbs...

14:09.580 --> 14:11.200
This is incredible!

14:12.070 --> 14:13.940
I'm glad you liked it.

14:14.250 --> 14:15.670
More!

14:18.250 --> 14:19.910
That was delicious.

14:19.910 --> 14:21.300
Thank you.

14:22.120 --> 14:24.460
I didn't expect you to 
eat three whole steaks.

14:24.460 --> 14:27.370
Maybe I should have, 
since you're the Fairy Queen's sister.

14:27.370 --> 14:31.390
Hey, if you're her sister, 
does that make you a fairy, too?

14:32.030 --> 14:34.800
No, I can't really talk about that.

14:34.800 --> 14:38.250
I also can't give you my real name.

14:38.250 --> 14:40.600
So just call me whatever you like.

14:40.600 --> 14:41.960
I see...

14:41.960 --> 14:43.750
I'll just call you "Ryuu" then.

14:44.180 --> 14:45.660
Ryuu?

14:45.660 --> 14:47.620
You've got those Japanese 
dragon-style horns.

14:47.620 --> 14:48.650
Or do you not like it?

14:49.730 --> 14:52.570
I never thought I'd get 
my own personal nickname.

14:52.570 --> 14:56.070
All right. You're the only one 
allowed to call me that!

14:56.070 --> 14:59.090
I plan on spending a lot of time around you!

14:59.090 --> 15:01.180
<i>The Fairy Queen's sister, huh?</i>

15:01.180 --> 15:04.430
<i>I hope she doesn't cause any more trouble...</i>

15:06.510 --> 15:08.920
<b>An Important Announcement
For All Players</b>

15:10.260 --> 15:12.140
Hey, Blacks!

15:12.140 --> 15:14.020
Oh, Earth!

15:14.020 --> 15:15.790
Did you see the official announcement?

15:15.790 --> 15:16.960
Yeah.

15:16.960 --> 15:19.100
Crazy stuff, huh?

15:19.520 --> 15:22.020
<b>An Important Announcement
For All Players</b>

15:19.880 --> 15:25.190
<i>It was an announcement about a previously 
hidden aspect of the game's design.</i>

15:25.930 --> 15:30.290
<i>Skills evolve by leveling them, 
which is how you learn arts.</i>

15:30.610 --> 15:36.240
<i>But there was a condition that needed to 
be met to learn the most powerful arts.</i>

15:36.600 --> 15:40.310
<i>You had to specialize in a single playstyle.</i>

15:40.760 --> 15:43.260
<i>If you wanted to use the 
most powerful physical arts,</i>

15:43.260 --> 15:46.360
<i>you needed to learn only 
physical attack skills.</i>

15:46.360 --> 15:48.870
<i>And if you wanted to learn 
the most powerful magic arts,</i>

15:48.870 --> 15:52.850
<i>you needed to learn only magical skills.</i>

15:54.390 --> 15:58.970
<i>It would've been one thing if that 
was just for combat skills, but...</i>

15:59.630 --> 16:02.790
I can't believe they made 
it apply to crafters, too.

16:03.730 --> 16:06.400
People are gonna be ticked 
off about this for a while.

16:06.690 --> 16:08.400
What are you going to do?

16:08.400 --> 16:12.180
They've given us a month 
to re-spec our skills.

16:12.180 --> 16:16.330
You might have trouble in the 
fights ahead if you don't.

16:16.630 --> 16:21.120
<i>Yeah, if I specialize in just physical attacks,</i>

16:21.120 --> 16:24.910
<i>it will probably give me 
more firepower in the end.</i>

16:24.910 --> 16:25.760
<i>But...</i>

16:26.750 --> 16:30.930
The style I've got now is 
what's most fun for me.

16:31.320 --> 16:32.890
So I'll keep things as they are now.

16:32.890 --> 16:34.360
I see, I see.

16:34.360 --> 16:38.440
All the guys who were only part-time 
crafters have been bailing out.

16:38.440 --> 16:43.460
With somebody like you around, though, 
it'll be a little less lonely.

16:44.420 --> 16:45.820
You're exaggerating.

16:46.310 --> 16:50.340
<i>Making people happy with delicious food 
is a kind of strength in its own.</i>

16:50.340 --> 16:53.230
<i>And I don't want to lose that strength.</i>

16:57.610 --> 16:58.740
Would you look at this?!

16:58.740 --> 16:59.880
What do you think?

16:59.880 --> 17:02.590
The materials you brought 
in were all high-quality,

17:02.590 --> 17:04.600
so I've got a lot of confidence in this one.

17:04.600 --> 17:06.080
This is great.

17:06.080 --> 17:08.370
My defense went way up.

17:08.370 --> 17:12.190
The bonuses to durability 
and psyche are great, too.

17:12.190 --> 17:14.310
Glad you like it.

17:14.680 --> 17:16.440
What will you do with the old armor?

17:16.440 --> 17:19.910
If you're going to just discard it, 
I can take it off your hands.

17:19.910 --> 17:23.830
No, it's been good to me for a long time.

17:23.830 --> 17:25.470
I want to give it a proper end myself.

17:26.310 --> 17:27.460
I see.

17:27.460 --> 17:30.190
It would make me happy if you 
took good care of your new armor,

17:30.190 --> 17:32.400
just like you did your old armor.

17:32.720 --> 17:34.320
Of course.

17:35.320 --> 17:39.340
<i>In this game, you can physically 
touch your equipment.</i>

17:39.800 --> 17:43.280
<i>Maybe that's why you get 
so attached to it,</i>

17:43.280 --> 17:46.080
<i>and feel a little sad when 
it's time to say goodbye.</i>

17:46.700 --> 17:49.280
<i>It's like meeting someone new, 
and then parting with them...</i>

17:51.610 --> 17:52.780
Earth.

17:55.310 --> 17:56.670
Queen?

17:56.980 --> 18:00.720
There's something I need to tell you.

18:02.140 --> 18:03.840
I'm putting up a barrier.

18:12.640 --> 18:14.320
First, I need to apologize.

18:14.680 --> 18:16.970
I'm so sorry...

18:16.970 --> 18:20.920
You will never be able to make 
a contract with a fairy.

18:20.920 --> 18:25.170
What? Do the fairies hate me that much?

18:26.550 --> 18:28.600
No, it's the opposite.

18:28.600 --> 18:32.100
The fairies love you too much!

18:32.690 --> 18:33.910
Huh?

18:34.270 --> 18:39.260
I was planning on introducing you to 
a fairy you could contract with soon.

18:39.670 --> 18:46.180
I planned to have you choose from one of 
the six greater fairies you see before you.

18:46.610 --> 18:50.800
We'd all love to make a contract with you.

18:50.800 --> 18:53.490
You're famous among fairies.

18:53.960 --> 18:59.440
But the citizens of the fairy 
kingdom found out about it.

18:59.440 --> 19:02.650
Over 80 percent of the country's 
population came to my gates

19:02.650 --> 19:06.790
and demanded to be allowed 
to make a contract with you.

19:07.350 --> 19:10.460
Th-That many?

19:10.950 --> 19:16.520
As queen of the fairy kingdom, 
I can't ignore the will of my people.

19:16.520 --> 19:22.580
If a fairy were to a contract with you, 
it would plunge the country into chaos.

19:22.900 --> 19:26.800
Oh, well... I understand, I guess.

19:27.110 --> 19:29.190
You're not upset?

19:29.190 --> 19:35.860
The lack of a contracted fairy will make 
your journeys and battles more difficult.

19:35.860 --> 19:38.390
Well, life's just like that sometimes.

19:38.390 --> 19:41.350
Who knows? Maybe it'll be fun to try it.

19:43.090 --> 19:46.140
You really are a strange man...

19:46.140 --> 19:51.030
Then, at the very least, allow me to give you 
another form of strength instead.

19:51.590 --> 19:53.370
Earth, give me your hand.

19:55.110 --> 19:57.210
I'll give you two powers.

19:57.440 --> 20:02.370
These two techniques are 
re-creations of powerful skills created

20:02.370 --> 20:05.480
in the time of the 21st Fairy Ruler.

20:07.010 --> 20:10.310
<b>Seven Falling Stars
Activates by landing seven consecutive shots on a target 
with a bow within 30 seconds of using the skill.
Once activated, damage to the target is greatly increased.</b>

20:07.440 --> 20:10.300
The first one is Seven Falling Stars.

20:10.580 --> 20:14.130
This looks like it'll be 
hard to learn to use.

20:14.130 --> 20:14.650
Yes.

20:15.260 --> 20:18.740
And the other is Sacrifice Bow.

20:15.730 --> 20:20.110
<b>Sacrifice Bow
Activates at the cost of 90% of Max HP, 100% of Max MP, and the
destruction of the currently equipped bow. Fires a powerful arrow.</b>

20:20.490 --> 20:23.020
This technique is extremely dangerous.

20:23.400 --> 20:28.090
It combines your life, your magic, 
and the feelings you placed into your bow,

20:28.090 --> 20:31.160
and fires a single, powerful arrow.

20:31.950 --> 20:36.930
It would be best not to use it 
except in the most dire of circumstances.

20:37.450 --> 20:38.520
Got it.

20:38.730 --> 20:43.320
The stats you lose will come 
back with proper rest.

20:43.320 --> 20:44.430
So don't worry.

20:45.070 --> 20:48.700
<i>But the weapon won't come back.</i>

20:48.700 --> 20:53.420
<i>So I have to decide if I'm willing to 
sacrifice a beloved weapon to fire it...</i>

20:54.550 --> 20:56.060
Got it.

20:56.060 --> 21:00.640
I don't know if I'll use Sacrifice Bow, 
but I'll practice with Seven Falling Stars.

21:00.640 --> 21:02.090
Good.

21:02.090 --> 21:04.980
Please, keep what I've told you a secret.

21:04.980 --> 21:08.060
Oh, and you've probably already 
seen the announcement, but...

21:09.160 --> 21:13.000
<b>The Fairy Kingdom is Coming
in the Next Update!</b>

21:09.420 --> 21:12.990
The path to the Fairy Kingdom will 
be opened to all you adventurers.

21:13.650 --> 21:15.080
The Fairy Kingdom?

21:15.080 --> 21:17.300
We'll be able to go after the next update?

21:17.300 --> 21:18.720
Yes!

21:18.720 --> 21:22.090
Please come see us when the path is opened.

21:22.090 --> 21:23.970
We'll all be happy to welcome you!

21:24.790 --> 21:27.100
I definitely will!

21:27.100 --> 21:29.920
Oh, let me give you all
 a present before you go.

21:30.550 --> 21:31.760
A present?

21:33.740 --> 21:37.650
Earth, thank you for this gift of food.

21:37.650 --> 21:39.940
I can't wait to try your cooking!

21:39.940 --> 21:40.750
Great.

21:41.290 --> 21:44.480
I guess I'll be seeing you 
in the Fairy Kingdom next.

21:44.480 --> 21:47.130
Oh, that might not be true!

21:47.890 --> 21:51.910
We might sneak out to come see you!

21:53.330 --> 21:55.750
Hey! Are you trying to come see 
him ahead of the rest of us?

21:55.750 --> 22:00.260
If anybody's at fault here, I think it's you, 
for keeping him all to yourself!

22:00.260 --> 22:02.940
I wanted to make a contract with him!

22:02.290 --> 22:04.150
<i>The Fairy Kingdom, huh?</i>

22:02.940 --> 22:04.240
Zephana!

22:04.150 --> 22:06.190
<i>Things are gonna get crazy, I bet.</i>

22:07.510 --> 22:09.970
<b>To Be Continued</b>
